Prohibition of manufacture of liquor and construction and working of distillery or
brewery.— No person shall—
(a) manufacture liquor;
(b) construct or work any distillery or brewery;
(c) import, export, transport or possess liquor; or
(d) sell or buy liquor.

No person shall—
(a) possess opium;
(b) transport opium;
(c) import or export opium;
(d) sell or buy opium; or
(e) consume or use opium.

The 2[State Government] may—
(a) establish a distillery in which spirit may be manufactured in accordance with a licence
issued under this Act on such conditions as the 3[State] Government deems fit to impose;
(b) discontinue any distillery established;
(c) licence, on such conditions as the 4[State] Government deems fit to impose the
construction and working of a distillery or brewery;
(d) establish or license a warehouse wherein any 5[intoxicant], hemp, mhowra flowers or
molasses may be deposited and kept without payment of duty; and
(e) discontinue any warehouse so established.

